    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "Forge Inheritor",
          "desc": "Basic Attacks restore Health and switch her weapons and combat forms. When hitting enemies with Basic Attacks or skills, she gains Attack Speed."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Peak-Crushing Polearm",
          "desc": "Dashes in the target direction, dealing damage to enemies in her path and launching them."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "World-Splitting Spear",
          "desc": "Thrusts forward in the target direction, dealing damage, knocking enemies back, and recovering Health."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Return of the Armsmaster",
          "desc": "Enhances herself, gaining Movement Speed and Attack Speed, and breaking the Fighting Spirit stack limit. Her Basic Attacks will also deal extra damage, and she will be able to use them while moving."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Strong duelist",
          "Very versatile",
          "Insane late-game damage"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Needs to ramp up passive",
          "Relies on ultimate for damage",
          "Melee form is weak"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nFor most of the Early Game, Chicha will be in melee form, which is her weakest state. You can use minions or jungle monsters to get 4 stacks of your passive, so once you go to the lane, you only need to auto-attack once, then use Skill 2 World-Splitting Spear to deal huge poke damage. Most of the Early Game will be you sitting underneath the tower last hitting minions, and waiting for your Overkill Form before looking to trade.\n\n## Teamfights\nBefore entering a teamfight, make sure to attack jungle monsters or minions to get 4 stacks. This is essential to Chicha's playstyle since her Overkill Form is what will win teamfights. Be patient with your Ultimate Return of the Armsmaster; wait for the right moment and target before using it for huge damage. You can use Skill 1 and Skill 2 during your Ultimate to help gap close and finish off enemies.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nAttack monsters or minions 4 times before joining a fight so you can enter Overkill Form straight away for maximum damage\nUse Skill 1 and Skill 2 before entering Overkill Form since the cooldown gets reduced\nAlways use Skill 2 as soon as you enter Overkill since it has a long cooldown\nMake sure to use the attack button when using your Ultimate to deal damage"
      }
    },
